$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Reference case: marina_float
$ Same domain and waves as marina_lay2 plus a FIXED rectangular pontoon
$ (30 m x 10 m, draft 1.5 m) given as a DRAFT input field.  Floating objects
$ require the semi-implicit scheme, so this case runs on the CPU path and is
$ the "fixed hull truth" against which the moving-pressure-patch vessel
$ representation of the bridge is compared.
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT 'marina' '02'
    'GPU regression: fixed floating pontoon'
    'implicit scheme, ILU preconditioner (icond=3 forced)'
    'generated by tests/cases/gen_inputs.py'
$
SET LEVEL 0. DEPMIN 0.001 MAXERR 3 SEED 12345 CARTESIAN
MODE DYNAMIC TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN
$
CGRID REGULAR 0. 0. 0. 200. 150. 200 150
VERTICAL 2
$
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0. 0. 0. 200 150 1. 1.
READINP BOTTOM 1. 'bot.dat' 3 0 FREE
$
INPGRID DRAFT REGULAR 0. 0. 0. 200 150 1. 1.
READINP DRAFT 1. 'draft.dat' 3 0 FREE
FLOAT 0. 1.0
$
INITIAL ZERO
$
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 SIG PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDCOND SIDE W CCW BTYPE WEAKREFL SMOOTHING 10 SEC CON SPECTRUM 0.8 6.0 0. 20. 600 SEC
SPONGELAYER E 30.
$
NONHYDROSTATIC BOX 1.0
BREAKING 0.6 0.3
FRICTION MANNING 0.019
TIMEI METHOD IMPLICIT 0.5 0.5
$
POINTS 'GAUGES' 40. 75. 80. 75. 120. 75. 160. 75. 100. 40.
TABLE 'GAUGES' NOHEAD 'gauges.tbl' TSEC WATL OUTPUT 000000.000 0.05 SEC
BLOCK 'COMPGRID' NOHEAD 'fields.mat' LAY 3 BOTL WATL VEL DRAF OUTPUT 000000.000 0.5 SEC
$ hydrodynamic loads on the pontoon (NOGRID table)
TABLE 'NOGRID' NOHEAD 'loads.tbl' TSEC FORCEX FORCEY FORCEZ MOMX MOMY MOMZ OUTPUT 000000.000 0.05 SEC
$
TEST 1 0
COMPUTE 000000.000 0.05 SEC 000100.000
STOP
